hats off to rassilon@eddie if you are still out there, "hi".

check out abermud from MIT.  it accomplishes the "hide from ps" (and
who) by doing an exec call on itself and changing arg[1].  it seems
that on some systems, arg[0] gets loaded and executed, and the
process table gets arg[1].  i tried this with nethack and was foiled
because nethack stat()'s arg[1] after chdir(). (if i am remembering
correctly)  i never tried to get further with this, but, ... maybe
this weekend.

the easy way around is simple, most players here symbolic link my
executable to a place easily accessible to them and (of course)
not called nethack.  h.out, run, update, and many others have recently
been seen cropping up.

as for getting rid of the "obvious" names, that is an option
when configuring before compiling.  change your playground to
~you/reports and save to ~you/reports/monthly and a simple change
will also change bones files to be "data.XX".

